From bb831e889bf57bcc22ef41bcf07970966849fb0f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: likailong <likailong5@huawei.com>
Date: Sun, 13 Sep 2026 23:11:46 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 01/14] [BugFix][Spec Decode] Skip EAGLE prefix-cache drop on
 PD producer for hybrid Mamba models

On a PD prefill producer every content-hash match is a verified prompt
block, so the EAGLE last-block drop in the hybrid KV cache coordinator is
never needed. With hybrid Mamba align pages (1536 tokens) the drop erases
the whole shared prefix of typical ~2K prompts: producer prefix hits are
pinned to 0 (1600-token prompts -> 0/0, 3200-token prompts -> 1536/3072
on the first full-attention group), the observed MTP prefix-cache kill
band.

* Derive the producer role from vllm_config.kv_transfer_config
  (is_kv_producer and not is_kv_consumer; kv_both keeps upstream behavior)
  and tag it onto KVCacheConfig in a wrapped
  get_kv_cache_config_from_groups. The tag survives the scheduler-side
  deepcopy and worker pickle IPC, and the coordinator factory can read it
  without receiving VllmConfig.
* AscendHybridKVCacheCoordinator reads the tag and skips the EAGLE block
  drop in both find_longest_cache_hit and
  find_longest_cache_hit_per_group; the EAGLE-group fallback marks
  FullAttention groups only.
* Add CPU-only unit tests for role tagging, the fallback gate and both
  producer lookup paths.

Signed-off-by: likailong <likailong5@huawei.com>
